    Call-by-Name:

   Here the expression is evaluated every time it is requested, no cache is stored.


    Call-by-Need:

   Here the expression is evaluated only once and it is stored for further reference, no cache is stored.


   In static scoping, the

    local variables have more preference than global variables

   if the name of both the variables is same. In dynamic scoping, the

    global variables are preferred over local variables.


